- Bootstrap Script(USER DATA)
A script that runs when the instance first runs
It passes user data to the EC2 instance and can be used to install applications as well as updates and more

bootstrap.sh -
#!/bin/bash
yum update -y
yum install httpd -y. // installs apache
yum service httpd start // starts apache
service httpd start
cd /var/www/html
echo "<html><body><h1>Hello cloud gurus</h1></body></html>" > index.html

Adding these tasks at boot time adds to the amount of time it takes to boot the instance. However, it allows you to automate the installation of applications

